== Washington implementation context
<washington-implementation-context>
RCW 28A.320.124 requires school-security policies covering limits on SRO
school discipline and family complaint processes. RCW 28A.320.1242
provides for annual review and adoption of agreements with law
enforcement or security providers, involving students, parents and
community members. RCW 9.41.360 creates liability in specified
unsafe-storage situations but expressly does not mandate how or where
every firearm must be stored. These statements are summaries, not legal
advice; have Washington counsel verify current law for each deployment.

== FERPA data firewall
<ferpa-data-firewall>
Department of Education guidance permits disclosure to external
threat-team members as school officials under particular conditions, but
use is purpose-limited and redisclosure restricted. A police officer's
team participation is not a general gateway into ordinary police
databases. Document lawful exceptions separately and log all
disclosures.

== Complaint and remedy protocol
<complaint-and-remedy-protocol>
+ Accept school, independent and external complaints, with accessible
  and confidential options.
+ Record allegations without presuming guilt; preserve evidence and
  exculpatory material.
+ Investigate through an independent reviewer when police or district
  leaders are implicated.
+ Notify families of determinations and available review or correction
  rights as applicable.
+ Publish anonymized complaint statistics, reasons for policy changes
  and suspension decisions.

#callout(warning: true)[
#strong[Oversight stop rules:] retaliatory referral, selection based on
protected speech or identity, unlawful searches or record transfers,
force beyond authorized roles, or AI-enabled automatic adverse action.
]
